# Worklog convention

This is Quentin's senior CS Independent Research repo (CARLA + RL, advised by Prof. Ozgur
Izmirli). Every branch other than `develop` has a running worklog at
`worklog/<branch-name>.md`, auto-created by a git `post-checkout` hook — see
`worklog/README.md`. It is Quentin's primary source material for mandatory weekly
progress reports to his advisor, and for PR descriptions — treat it as a real part of the
task, not optional overhead.

When helping with development on a branch, append a dated entry to that branch's worklog
file whenever a meaningful change happens: something gets implemented, an experiment
runs, a bug is hit, something fails, a result comes back. Do this proactively as work
happens, not only when asked. Format and an example are in `worklog/_TEMPLATE.md`. Skip
trivial/mechanical changes (typos, formatting).

When a PR is being opened, draw on the worklog to fill out
`.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` rather than writing those sections from scratch.

For git branching/commit conventions, see `CONTRIBUTING.md`. For full research context,
see `MASTER_CARLA_RESEARCH_SUMMARY.md`.
